# ==============================================================================
# FILE: .dockerignore
# ARCHITECTURE ROLE: Docker Context Filtering & Secret Protection
#
# 🎓 BEGINNER'S GUIDE TO .dockerignore:
#   What does this file do?
#     When you run `docker build .`, Docker packages the current folder and uploads
#     it into the Docker Daemon (called the "Build Context").
#     If you don't ignore files:
#       1. Your build upload will be slow because it sends hundreds of megabytes of `node_modules`.
#       2. You might accidentally bake private `.env.local` API keys or passwords into public images!
#     This file tells Docker: "DO NOT copy these files or folders into the container."
# ==============================================================================

# Dependencies (Installed fresh inside the Linux container)
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Next.js build output (Rebuilt cleanly inside the container)
.next
out

# Git version control files
.git
.gitignore

# Environment files containing local secrets
.env*.local
.env.development
.env.test

# IDE and OS metadata files
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Docker configuration files
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
